---
import MediaSlot from '../MediaSlot.astro';
import BrowserArt from '../art/BrowserArt.astro';
import Logo from '../Logo.astro';
const tools = ['open_browser_page', 'navigate_page', 'click_element', 'type_in_page', 'hover_element', 'drag_element', 'handle_dialog', 'read_page', 'screenshot_page', 'run_playwright_code'];
---
<section class="section feature" id="browser" aria-labelledby="browser-title">
	<div class="container split">
		<div class="copy head">
			<p class="eyebrow">05 — Integrated browser</p>
			<h2 id="browser-title">The agent can see <span class="muted">the page too.</span></h2>
			<p class="lede">
				A Playwright-backed browser lives inside the editor, and the agent gets its tools — thirty-eight in all,
				on by default. Open a page, navigate, click, type, hover, read the page's accessibility tree, take a
				screenshot, run Playwright code: the loop from change to check closes without leaving the editor.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="demo">
			<MediaSlot name="browser-tools" label="The integrated browser in Sirius showing a local page, beside the agent's tool runs: open_browser_page, click_element, read_page, screenshot_page."><BrowserArt /></MediaSlot>
		</div>
		<div class="copy more">
			<ul class="points">
				<li><Logo size={20} class="pt-icon" /><div><b>Read first, look when it helps.</b> <code>read_page</code> returns the accessibility snapshot, which any text model can use; <code>screenshot_page</code> reaches the models that accept images.</div></li>
				<li><Logo size={20} class="pt-icon" /><div><b>Real Playwright underneath.</b> Dialogs, drag and drop, hover states and arbitrary Playwright code are all there — the same engine your end-to-end tests use.</div></li>
				<li><Logo size={20} class="pt-icon" /><div><b>Offered where it fits.</b> The browser family sits in the agent's extended tool tier, so a small local model is not handed sixteen schemas it cannot hold.</div></li>
			</ul>
			<p class="chips" aria-label="Browser tools">{tools.map((t) => <code class="chip">{t}</code>)}</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.05fr); grid-template-areas: "head demo" "more demo"; column-gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5.5rem); row-gap: 1.75rem; align-items: center; }
	.head { grid-area: head; align-self: end; }
	.more { grid-area: more; align-self: start; }
	.demo { grid-area: demo; }
	.copy h2 { margin-top: 1rem; }
	.copy .lede { margin-top: 1.25rem; font-size: var(--text-m); }
	.points { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
	.points li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 20px 1fr; gap: 0.85rem; align-items: start; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: var(--text-s); line-height: 1.55; }
	.points b { color: var(--fg); }
	.points :global(.pt-icon) { margin-top: 0.3em; }
	.chips { margin-top: 1.5rem; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem; }
	.chip { font-size: var(--text-xs); padding: 0.25em 0.6em; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); color: var(--fg-muted); }
	@media (max-width: 900px) { .split { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); grid-template-areas: "head" "demo" "more"; row-gap: 2.25rem; } }
</style>
